      "text": "Organized crime is sustained criminal enterprise -- groups that use violence, corruption, and organizational structure to run illegal markets or extract resources. The key analytical challenge: it resists easy categorization because it ranges from hierarchical bureaucracies to fluid network arrangements, and it constantly adapts to law enforcement pressure."
